          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Just as the notion of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            generalizes that of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+in+a+monoidal+category"} monoid in a monoidal category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+over+a+monoid"} modules over monoids
            generalize easily to modules over monads.
          %p
            Beware that modules over monads in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            are often called
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+a+monad"} *algebras* for the monad
            (see there for more), since they literally are algebras in the sense of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+algebra"} universal algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#AlgebrasForMonadsInCat"} below
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            as “algebras for the monad”.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formally dual
            concept is that of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coalgebra+over+a+comonad"} coalgebra over a comonad
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#modules Modules
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \colon a \to a
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            with structure 2-cells
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi t
                  %mi t
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu \colon t t \Rightarrow t
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi a
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta \colon 1_a \Rightarrow t
            %strong
              left
              = succeed "-module" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            (or
            = succeed ")" do
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
                \-algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi b
                  %mo →
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \colon b \to a
            and a 2-cell
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi t
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda \colon t x \Rightarrow x
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi t
                          %mi t
                          %mi x
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mi μ
                              %mi x
                        %mtd
                          %mi t
                          %mi x
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi t
                          %mi λ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mi λ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi t
                          %mi x
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo →
                            %mi λ
                        %mtd
                          %mi x
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi x
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mi η
                              %mi x
                        %mtd
                          %mi t
                          %mi x
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mi λ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  t t x &amp; \overset{\mu x}{\to} &amp; t x \\
                  t\lambda\downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow \lambda \\
                  t x &amp; \underset{\lambda}{\to} &amp; x
                  }
                  \\qquad \qquad
                  \\array{
                  x &amp; \overset{\eta x}{\to} &amp; t x \\
                  \&amp; 1\searrow &amp; \downarrow \lambda \\
                  \&amp; &amp; x
                  }
          %p
            commute. Similarly, a
            %strong
              right
              = succeed "-module" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            (or
            = succeed ")" do
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
                \-opalgebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \colon a \to c
            and a 2-cell
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi y
                    %mi t
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho \colon y t \Rightarrow y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            on the left instead of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            on the right.
          %p
            Clearly, a right
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            is the same thing as a left
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^{\mathrm{op}}
            %strong
              left
              = succeed "-comodule" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            or
            %strong coalgebra
            is then a left
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} co
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^{\mathrm{co}}
            %strong
              right
              = succeed "-comodule" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            is a left
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} coop
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^{\mathrm{coop}}
          %p
            A
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            %em a fortiori
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+an+endomorphism"} algebra over the underlying endomorphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
          %h3#bimodules Bimodules
          %p
            Given monads
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s,t
              \-bimodule
            is given by a 1-cell
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi b
                    %mo →
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\colon b \to a
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi x
                  %mi s
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho \colon x s \Rightarrow x
            and a left
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi t
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda \colon t x \Rightarrow x
            that are compatible in the sense that the diagram
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi t
                          %mi x
                          %mi s
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mi t
                              %mi ρ
                        %mtd
                          %mi t
                          %mi x
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi λ
                          %mi s
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mi λ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi x
                          %mi s
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo →
                            %mi ρ
                        %mtd
                          %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  t x s &amp; \overset{t\rho}{\to} &amp; t x \\
                  \\lambda s \downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow \lambda \\
                  x s &amp; \underset{\rho}{\to} &amp; x
                  }
          %p
            commutes. Such a bimodule may be written as
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi s
                    %mi ⇸
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \colon s &amp;#8696; t
          %p
            A
            %strong morphism
            of left
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi λ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi λ
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,\lambda) \to (x',\lambda')
            is given by a 2-cell
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi x
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \colon x \Rightarrow x'
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi t
                    %mi α
                    %mo =
                    %mi α
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda' \circ t\alpha = \alpha \circ \lambda
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (y,\rho) \to (y',\rho')
            is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi y
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi y
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta \colon y \Rightarrow y'
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi α
                    %mi s
                    %mo =
                    %mi α
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho' \circ \alpha s = \alpha \circ \rho
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi λ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi λ
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,\lambda,\rho) \to (x',\lambda',\rho')
            is given by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi x
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \colon x \Rightarrow x'
            that is a morphism of both left and right modules.
          %p
            More abstractly, the monads
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            give rise to ordinary monads
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi s
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s^*
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t_*
            on the hom-category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(b,a)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            then gives rise to an invertible
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+law"} distributive law
            between these, so that the composite
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
