            This again satisfies standard equations stating compatibility with the monad structure on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
          %p
            A
            %em right module
            is equipped with a binary map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊲
                  %mo :
                  %mi m
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                  %mo →
                  %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lhd : m, t \to m
            instead, and a bimodule has a ternary map
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊳
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ⊲
                    %mo :
                    %mi t
                    %mo ,
                    %mi m
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mo →
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rhd - \lhd : t,m,t \to m
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#colimits Colimits
          %p
            see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits+in+categories+of+algebras"} colimits in categories of algebras
          %h3#tensor_product Tensor product
          %p
            Given bimodules
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi r
                  %mi ⇸
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x' \colon r &amp;#8696; s
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi s
                    %mi ⇸
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \colon s &amp;#8696; t
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo ,
                  %mi s
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r,s,t
            are monads on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c,b,a
            respectively, we may be able to form the
            %strong tensor product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi s
                  %mi x
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi r
                  %mi ⇸
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \otimes_s x' \colon r &amp;#8696; t
            just as in the case of bimodules over rings. If the hom-categories of the bicategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            have
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflexive+coequalizer"} reflexive coequalizer
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(c,a)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi x
                          %mi s
                          %mi x
                          %mo ′
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi x
                          %mi x
                          %mo ′
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                          %mi x
                          %msub
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi s
                          %mi x
                          %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  x s x' &amp; \overset{\to}{\to} &amp; x x' &amp; \to x \otimes_s x'
                  }
          %p
            where the parallel arrows are the two induced actions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mi x
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho x'
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mi λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \lambda
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            the forgetful functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Mod
                    %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi r
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi r
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_K(r,t) = K(c,a)^{r^* t_*} \to K(c,a)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits+in+categories+of+algebras"} reflects reflexive coequalizers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r^* t_*
            preserves them, and so
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi s
                  %mi x
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \otimes_s x'
            is an
            = succeed "-bimodule." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r,t
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            satisfies the above conditions then there is a bicategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod(K)
            consisting of monads, bimodules and bimodule morphisms in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            itself, and the unit and associativity conditions follow from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            of the above coequalizer. There is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+functor"} lax
            forgetful functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod(K) \to K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_a \to t
            the unit of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mi x
                  %mo ′
                  %mo →
                  %mi x
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi s
                  %mi x
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x x' \to x \otimes_s x'
            the coequalizer map.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            If
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo =
                    %mi Span
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K = Span(Set)
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} span
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            is precisely a small category. Then
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi Prof
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod(K) = Prof
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctor"} profunctor
          %p
            More generally,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Span
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod(Span(C))
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            any category with coequalizers and pullbacks that preserve them, consists of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category"} internal categories
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+profunctor"} internal profunctors
            between them and transformations between those.
